{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/205376-homebrew-demon-translation-lexicon","id":205376,"title":"Homebrew Demon Translation Lexicon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-22T15:16:07-07:00","id":205376,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Homebrew Demon Translation Lexicon","content":"I know I'm doing this prematurely, but I wanted help making a translation guide for people who want to convert the technological terms into more archaic/arcane terms. It's actually proving to be really hard to do, since I don't want to confuse people with poorly chosen replacement words. Also don't know how much needs to be altered to get the approval of people from either side of the fandom. Please help me!<br /> <br /> Here's all I've gotten so far:<br /> <br /> <i>Agendas:</i><br /> Inquisitor<br /> Integrator -- Reconcilor<br /> Saboteur -- Ravager<br /> Tempter<br /> <br /> Embeds -- Hymns? Lores?<br /> Exploits --<br /> <br /> <i>Demonic Form:</i><br /> Modifications -- Mutations<br /> Technologies -- Sorceries?<br /> Processes --<br /> Propulsion --<br /> <br /> Cipher -- Malapraxis?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T20:17:19-07:00","id":205562,"title":"","content":"Inquisitors are Cryptics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T20:55:03-07:00","id":205625,"title":"","content":"Tempters are likewise Faustians, if you're borrowing from the Fallen terms, in which case the Saboteurs are properly the Rav<b>en</b>ers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T21:46:08-07:00","id":205644,"title":"","content":"Kind of hard since the factions have overlapping goals. Faustians are some kind of tempter/saboteur duel agenda, Raveners are pure Saboteurs except for the weirdoes who are Saboteur/Integrator, Cryptics are probably every dual agenda that includes Inquisitor, the Reconcillers are the simplest at pure Integrator through and through and the Luciferans are loosely Saboteur but have such a hyper focused goal that they might be better off as some kind of niche agenda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1266-sirpants","name":"SirPants","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T05:02:55-07:00","id":205954,"title":"","content":"I would have Embeds be &quot;Chapters&quot; and Exploits be &quot;Verses&quot; as Angels are the embodiments of the Word and the Word is God. Following that same theme I would name the Cipher, &quot;The Word&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T05:47:30-07:00","id":205965,"title":"","content":"The <b>Descent</b> Agendas map reasonably well to four of the <b>Fallen</b> Factions. This much works whichever way you\u2019re translating. If translating from <b>Fallen</b> to <b>Descent</b>, the fifth Faction (the Luciferans) is too specifically tied into the cWoD metaplot to have any parallel in nWoD: to do them justice in nWoD, you\u2019d need to port over a Lucifer-like figure for them to be searching for. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure what terminology I\u2019d use when grafting Embeds and Exploits into <b>Fallen</b>. \u201cChapter\u201d and \u201cVerse\u201d are perhaps a bit too clich\u00e9. More generally, I\u2019m not sure how well Embeds and Exploits would work in <b>Fallen</b> <i>at all</i>; conceptually, they\u2019re a bit too tied into the \u201ctechgnostic\u201d flavor of Descent, given their linguistic, quantum, and similar conceptual roots. <br /> <br /> The one I\u2019m most curious about, though, is how <b>Fallen</b>\u2019s Houses and <b>Descent</b>\u2019s Incarnations would map to the other game. Do four of the Houses map directly to the Incarnations, much like the Factions and Agendas above? Or is it messier than that? This matters when assigning Embeds and Exploits to the Fallen, or Lores to the Unchained: who gets which types? If three Houses translate as entirely new Incarnations, does that mean we need three whole new sets of Embeds and Exploits? <br /> <br /> Though frankly, if I were transplanting elements of <b>Demon: the Fallen</b> into nWoD terms, the Unchained aren\u2019t who I\u2019d go to first as recipients of those grafts. Rather, I\u2019d target the Possessed, from <b>Inferno</b>. They\u2019re a much better nWoD counterpart to the Fallen than the Unchained are. In that regard, I\u2019d probably try to draw rough parallels between <b>Fallen</b>\u2019s Houses and the Seven Deadly Sins that are the closest thing the Possessed have to x-splats. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T07:01:13-07:00","id":206041,"title":"","content":"It was my assumption that we weren't translating them into Fallen but removing the technological aspects to make Descent a more traditional-styled demon game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T07:14:32-07:00","id":206059,"title":"","content":"Working under the assumption that we're still talking about changing the technological elements of <i>Demon: the Descent </i>so that they are more archaic/arcane. I felt my suggestion of Chapter and Verse wasn't terribly cliche simply because more traditional angels are sometimes thought to communicate not through language (that is verbal or somatic cues ascribed meaning by the human consensus) but by intent (that is conceptual meaning). This concept seems fairly in line with the otherwise esoteric nature of Embeds and Exploits.<br /> <br /> Now if we're converting <i>Demon: the Fallen</i> into <i>Demon: the Descent </i>I think that embeds and exploits are probably best placed aside in favour of conversion of the Lores from that game. My group and I did a homebrew conversion of our own using the Mage arcana as a starting point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T07:16:48-07:00","id":206060,"title":"","content":"If that\u2019s the case, then there\u2019s no need to rename the Agendas. The only things needing new names would be \u201cGadget\u201d, \u201cEmbed\u201d, \u201cExploit\u201d, and the various Demonic Form ability types.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T08:12:38-07:00","id":206125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/205376-homebrew-demon-translation-lexicon?p=206060#post206060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that\u2019s the case, then there\u2019s no need to rename the Agendas. The only things needing new names would be \u201cGadget\u201d, \u201cEmbed\u201d, \u201cExploit\u201d, and the various Demonic Form ability types.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that and Infrastructure.<br /> <br /> But yes, we're just trying to get rid of the techno-theme and go for a more arcane style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T08:52:39-07:00","id":206180,"title":"","content":"Infrastructure could be fluffed as &quot;Holy Ground&quot;. There are a few ways you could then define it. You could make <i>actual </i>consecrated ground the only infrastructure in your game world but the problem with that is that infrastructure is assumed to be more common than that. However an easy way to resolve this issue is to suggest that any sense of genuine, selfless community or territory can cause &quot;holy ground&quot;. Anywhere people band together to make a difference - if you're assuming that your God (minus Machine) is a positive force. Or, if you're assuming that your God (minus the Machine) is a neutral (or negative) force like the gnostic demiurge then you could suggest that He works through any sense of community that He personally has a hand in creating and so consecrates those grounds simply through their existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T08:59:46-07:00","id":206184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/205376-homebrew-demon-translation-lexicon?p=206180#post206180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Infrastructure could be fluffed as &quot;Holy Ground&quot;. There are a few ways you could then define it. You could make <i>actual </i>consecrated ground the only infrastructure in your game world but the problem with that is that infrastructure is assumed to be more common than that. However an easy way to resolve this issue is to suggest that any sense of genuine, selfless community or territory can cause &quot;holy ground&quot;. Anywhere people band together to make a difference - if you're assuming that your God (minus Machine) is a positive force. Or, if you're assuming that your God (minus the Machine) is a neutral (or negative) force like the gnostic demiurge then you could suggest that He works through any sense of community that He personally has a hand in creating and so consecrates those grounds simply through their existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, we can't say it like that. Because we shouldn't make it seem like the god they're fighting is pure good (especially if you want to keep demons sympathetic). How about Infrastructure being more akin to focal points of power? Or arcane structures built and disguised by the advanced powers of the Angelic Host?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T11:23:24-07:00","id":206337,"title":"","content":"Worth noting: the &quot;Infra-&quot; part of &quot;Infrastructure&quot; shares an etymological root with &quot;Inferno.&quot; It's no accident that a lot of it is underground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T12:36:56-07:00","id":206458,"title":"","content":"Another problem I'm having is trying to figure out how to explain new demons coming into being if the God-Machine (Demiurge/God) is no longer building them like robots or biomorphs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T12:47:38-07:00","id":206465,"title":"","content":"That rather steps beyond the domain of a change in nomenclature. Components both abstract and concrete go in, angels come out. You don't need to explain that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T13:20:01-07:00","id":206484,"title":"","content":"So what would you call it then? Occult-matrix sounds too modern and technical a term... or is it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T13:29:55-07:00","id":206490,"title":"","content":"Another etymology lesson: &quot;matrix&quot; comes from the same root as &quot;matron&quot; \u2014 the term's original Latin meaning referred to a breeding female, but later came to refer to a <i>womb</i>; the modern definitions of the term include a mold that gives something its shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-23-2014, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T02:07:07-07:00","id":206833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/205376-homebrew-demon-translation-lexicon?p=206465#post206465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That rather steps beyond the domain of a change in nomenclature. Components both abstract and concrete go in, angels come out. You don't need to explain that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I couldn't agree more with you.<br /> <br /> On the note of infrastructure then perhaps renaming it to something more esoteric and arcane, like you suggest. I would perhaps recommend something to do with the concept of the &quot;fundament&quot; or &quot;foundation&quot; since infrastructure is still functionally used to bring angelic forces into the world or otherwise allow the demiurge control. So it would be a point of foundation, perhaps infrastructure could be referred to as a pillar? Admittedly, I'm grasping at straws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T01:19:04-07:00","id":208001,"title":"","content":"Due to the musical nature of some nomenclature, maybe go with Verses, but instead of chapters, have Songs? I do like Fundament for infrastructure, as it fits and has biblical flavor. Id call aether Hellfire (in fact, i often use that in my games, though only in the flavor description not usually as a word modern demons use), or perhaps Faith. Occult matrix could be Miracle. Going loud could be called taking apocalyptic form. Gadgets.. Reliquaries, maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T08:27:48-07:00","id":208355,"title":"","content":"Should we keep the term bolthole? We could also try manses, but I'm not sure if it's necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T11:03:15-07:00","id":208477,"title":"","content":"Sanctuary has a sort of churchly vibe to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T11:15:42-07:00","id":208489,"title":"","content":"But Mages already have sanctuary as a merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T19:25:17-07:00","id":208965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/205376-homebrew-demon-translation-lexicon?p=208489#post208489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Mages already have sanctuary as a merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Sanctum,&quot; identical root notwithstanding, is a different word than &quot;sanctuary.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T22:42:46-07:00","id":209082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/205376-homebrew-demon-translation-lexicon?p=206041#post206041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was my assumption that we weren't translating them into Fallen but removing the technological aspects to make Descent a more traditional-styled demon game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd really like to see what the God-Machine was like before the modern era. I'd be really happy if Demon's <i>Dark Era</i> took place in Venice or during the Crusades or something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/205376-homebrew-demon-translation-lexicon?p=206458#post206458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another problem I'm having is trying to figure out how to explain new demons coming into being if the God-Machine (Demiurge/God) is no longer building them like robots or biomorphs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they could still be built, but less like robots and more like Warforged or golem. The whole molded out of clay myth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T08:32:35-07:00","id":209350,"title":"","content":"I agree Aspel, I would be thrilled if the <i>Dark Era</i> for Demon was the Crusades, Biblical period or general Middle-Ages. It'd be very interesting to see if they keep the futurist vibe of Demons to maintain their alien nature and detail whether humans simply react out of ignorance or if the God-Machine itself somehow metaphysically reflects the era because it is always the collective idea of &quot; a complex machine&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T10:19:53-07:00","id":209384,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking about taking a stab at this on and off since this thread was posted. Today I have time to think about it! So let's browse around.<br /> <br /> We need to divide this, I think, into two approaches: historical descriptions of the Unchained in the New World of Darkness, and terms usable to adopt or merge Demon: the Fallen with Demon: the Descent. I don't think the product will come out as well if it tries to serve two masters. I'll come back to the latter half of this later. For now, the former, for which I'm trying to unify the Unchained's tendency to adopt plain language with the flavor of premodernity; I'm also trying to keep from making it very culturally specific, such that translated terms can be found in different parts of the world, and to avoid too much overlap with other nWoD mechanical terms, though I have less priority in avoiding certain kinds of terms (secondary monikers for Awakened Paths: &quot;theurge&quot;) than others (I really wanted to make the Technologies &quot;Manifestations,&quot; but doubling up on the name for another template's major power was too close for comfort).<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Historical Descent:</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>Inquisitors: </b>Monitors.<br /> <b>Integrators: </b>Theurges.<br /> <b>Saboteurs: </b>Militants.<br /> <b>Tempters: </b>Hedonists.<br /> <b>Agendas: </b>Approaches.<br /> <b>Agencies:</b> Guilds.<br /> <br /> <b>Embeds: </b>Formulas.<br /> <b>Exploits: </b>Deviations.<br /> <b>Interlocks: </b>Inferences.<br /> <b>Ciphers:</b> Mysteries.<br /> <b>Gadgets: </b>Curios.<br /> <br /> <b>Modifications:</b> Transfigurations.<br /> <b>Technologies:</b> Projections.<br /> <b>Propulsions:</b> Conveyances.<br /> <b>Processes:</b> Countenances.<br /> <br /> <b>Infrastructure:</b> Assemblies.<br /> <b>Facilities: </b>Reliquaries.<br /> <b>Occult matrices: </b>Divine workings.<br /> <b>Output:</b> Ends.<br /> <b>Projects:</b> Ministries.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T14:24:54-07:00","id":566985,"title":"","content":"&quot;Later&quot; turned out to be a year. <i>Oops.</i><br /> <br /> In recasting the names of the Agendas of DtD for the Fallen, I borrowed the names of the Factions, for obvious reasons. However, in doing so, I chose names that map onto the Agendas without concern for whether the Faction with that original name corresponds to the new Agenda. For this reason, I know some may object to ill fits, and so I provided alternative names. You can also assign Faction names as you prefer, of course.<br /> <br /> Did I miss anything important?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Descent in Fallen Terms:</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Inquisitors:</b> Cryptics, or Watchers.<br /> <b>Integrators:</b> Reconcilers, or Penitents.<br /> <b>Saboteurs:</b> Luciferans, or Judges.<br /> <b>Tempters:</b> Faustians, or Princes.<br /> <b>Agendas:</b> Factions.<br /> <b>Agencies:</b> Parliaments.<br /> <br /> <b>Embeds:</b> Evocations.<br /> <b>Exploits:</b> Conjuries.<br /> <b>Interlocks:</b> Contemplations.<br /> <b>Ciphers:</b> Logia, or Words.<br /> <b>Gadgets:</b> Relics.<br /> <br /> <b>Aether:</b> Pneuma, or Breath.<br /> <b>Primum:</b> Hypostasis.<br /> <br /> <b>Demonic Form Abilities:</b> As Historical Descent.<br /> <br /> <b>Infrastructure:</b> Congregations.<br /> <b>Facilities:</b> Sanctuaries.<br /> <b>Occult matrices:</b> Miracles.<br /> <b>Output:</b> Apparitions.<br /> <b>Projects:</b> Workings.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T18:29:27-07:00","id":567212,"title":"","content":"D<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/205376-homebrew-demon-translation-lexicon?p=209350#post209350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree Aspel, I would be thrilled if the <i>Dark Era</i> for Demon was the Crusades, Biblical period or general Middle-Ages. It'd be very interesting to see if they keep the futurist vibe of Demons to maintain their alien nature and detail whether humans simply react out of ignorance or if the God-Machine itself somehow metaphysically reflects the era because it is always the collective idea of &quot; a complex machine&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Neolithic Demon:</b> Thog make Gadget of sharp rock. It cut good, but it look weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T18:37:18-07:00","id":567217,"title":"","content":"Especially clever neolithic demons have learned to encode Embeds and Exploits into patterns of grooves while working malleable clays, before firing them for pottery. They can then run set needles along the grooves to activate these so-called &quot;software gadgets.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user"